#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# cycle_index_polynomial

#% text
# `cycle_index_polynomial(G, x)`: the cycle index (1/|G|) sum over g of prod x(k)^(number of k-cycles of g)

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Each element contributes the product of x(k)^(number of its cycles of length k) on the points 1, ..., n of the group.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
cycle_index_polynomial(cyclic_group(4), x)
#% output
#= (1/4)*x(1)^4 + (1/4)*x(2)^2 + (1/2)*x(4)

#% cell
cycle_index_polynomial(symmetric_group(3), z)
#% output
#= (1/6)*z(1)^3 + (1/3)*z(3) + (1/2)*z(1)*z(2)

